video
 * drv3DfxVoodooVSA - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvATIMach64
 * drvATIRage
 * drvCirrusLogicGD5434 - builds and links against the reference binary, 19/21 functions byte-identical, apple-generic version bundle present, SGS VERS_STRING/VERS_NUM unmet, setMode: and setPCIConfiguration unmatched; not hardware-tested
 * drvIBMThinkPad760EDDisplay - reconstructed against the reference binary, built, ledger advanced; not hardware-tested
 * drvMatroxMGA - complete
 * drvNVidiaRiva - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvS3Generic - complete
 * drvVBE20DisplayDriver - reconstructed against Apple's VBE20DisplayDriver_reloc from OPENSTEP 4.2 User Patch 4, the only driver in the tree reconstructed against a different OS release; 15 partition entries, 13 hand-written and all 13 byte-identical in place, __cstring and __data byte-identical, whole __text differs in 3 raw bytes, all in the two build-generated Kernel Server methods (the _VBE20DisplayDriver_instance common the reference leaves unallocated, and IO_DRIVERKIT_VERSION 420 there against 500 here); builds and links. Boot gate passed 2026-09-22 against the kernel that exports _VBEModeInfo2IODisplayInfo (spec 2): sarld links it as a Boot Driver, it takes the "card not in VBE mode" path and registers as VBEDisplay0, with no other boot driver lost (a weak check by itself, since this driver links last); a kernel without the symbol fails its link with "rld(): Undefined symbols" as predicted and does not panic, though with the driver linked last neither the predicted cascade nor its panic could show; that neither would at other positions is inferred from rld.c, not measured (docs/kernel/i386-vbe-console.md) [refuted for the first position by spec 3's G5, 2026-09-23: linked first, its failed link makes the next one fail with "rld(): virtual memory exhausted", every later boot driver is refused, and the kernel panics "Missing EISA kernel bus class"; the same driver linked first on a kernel with the symbol, under the same stock booter and sarld, loses nothing, so the failed link and not the order sets it off, by a mechanism not determined; qualified after the final review: those two runs also differ in kernel, the negative-control one being 4,168 bytes smaller for reasons spec 2 left unrecorded]. The framebuffer path waits on the booter [done: in spec 3's gates, 2026-09-23, our booter set VBE mode 257 on QEMU and the driver took its "using VBE mode 257" path, listing every recorded mode, while the kernel console drew through the frame buffer; getCharValues: and the Window Server untested]; not hardware-tested
 * drvVBoxVideo - complete
 * drvVGA - both halves reconstructed against Apple's binaries; VGA_reloc 29 of 38 ledger entries assembly-matched with 6 control-flow-confirmed, VGA_psdrvr 34 of 53 with the other 19 linker and dyld glue; emu486 is hand-written assembly, transcribed rather than decompiled, and assembles to the reference's exact 10496 bytes with every differing byte an address field off by a constant link displacement. Builds clean, no missing strings or symbols either half, every section matching bar __TEXT,__const's build-generated version strings. Boot-tested 2026-09-20 with the rebuilt kernel, which the stock one blocks by dying in the open EIDE defect first: registers VGADisplay0, sets the VGA mode from Default.table and the VESA mode from SVGABIOS.table with the emulator driving a real-mode INT 10h, renders the GUI at 800x600 in 2bpp and round-trips the cursor pixel-exactly over 110 motion events. Reaches the same desktop as part of a fully reconstructed stack with our kernel, drvPCIBus and drvEISABus, all four binaries hash-verified in place first. Not hardware-tested
 * drvVMWareVideo - complete

other - (these live at src/drvBPF and src/drvPortServer, not under drivers-i386)
 * drvBPF - reconstructed against the reference binary, fixes applied, not yet compiled or tested
 * drvPortServer - reconstructed against the reference binary, five pre-existing compile blockers repaired, fixes applied, not yet compiled or tested
